## Hard constraints

- NEVER write to competitor sites or AI services — read-only observation
- NEVER expose Kushal's logged-in session details, cookies, or PII
- NEVER scrape competitor sites at rates > 1 request per second (be polite)
- ALWAYS cache snapshots so we don't re-query DataForSEO unnecessarily (cost)
- ALWAYS post Slack — even if nothing changed
- If Claude in Chrome can't reach an AI service: skip + flag, don't error out

## Coordination

- Runs Thursday 7 PM IST — well clear of morning cron cluster
- Reads competitor list from `brain/COMPETITORS.md` (manually maintained by Kushal or via Meta-Learner proposal)
- Reads AI priority queries from `brain/AI-PRIORITY-QUERIES.md`
- Writes intelligence to brain/memory/ + BACKLOG
- Strategist's Friday 8 PM run will read this data + adjust BACKLOG priorities

## First-run note

This is the inaugural run, so there's no "last week's snapshot" to diff. Skip Step 4's diff logic, just establish baseline. Note `BASELINE_RUN: true` in the report. Next Thursday will have a real comparison.

If competitor DataForSEO data isn't accessible (subscription tier issue), use a simpler signal: just fetch competitor sitemaps + count URLs. Coarser but reliable.

If Claude in Chrome isn't connected to the Mac Mini browser, post `⚠ Chrome MCP not connected — install Claude-in-Chrome extension` and skip AI citation checks (still do competitive watch).
